  "defect": "Advisory stat false absence at the initial inspection and final reinspection makes the legacy root-journal-only cleaner delete independently checkpoint-owned or peer-queue-accepted packs. Stopping all participants does not revoke their references.",
  "fix": "Fresh read-only opens of storage.log and queues reject shared layouts without reading their contents; non-NotFound errors raise UnsafeRecovery. cleanup_orphans retains stopped-run gating and full report reinspection/comparison.",
  "findings": [
    "Four hosts run 64 baseline and 64 fixed cases across catalog/queue layouts, 2 KiB/8 MiB payloads, stat ENOENT/EIO and open EIO/EACCES. Baseline stat false absence deletes 16 protected packs totaling 67,144,696 bytes. All fixed cases preserve data and refuse unsafe inspection/cleanup.",
    "Baseline Python 3.12 stat EIO already raises OSError and does not delete data. Baseline open faults remain unused because stat sees the shared marker. Fixed stat arms remain unused; fixed open EIO/EACCES faults are consumed and rejected.",
    "Checkpoint owners or accepted peer WALs survive the baseline unsafe deletion. These are private controlled reproductions, not naturally observed filesystem faults.",
    "Catalog fixtures explicitly release their owner before normal GC; legacy namespace fixtures use separately reported private teardown. Already unsafely deleted files are never counted as normal GC."
  ],
  "source_binding": {
    "src/straw/inspect.py": "ba81adc666b4c4334fa90a68f02a547e3cbdb17d398e59757bc152e7589dcfa4",
    "tests/test_offline_inspection.py": "7f03871ffd8e1537bb5163ff489dafe7df8b10bf0f44ce9bb4928f93e93ef683",
    "verification/offline_guard_probe.py": "0c0d1412c9a9d552f0821553870227cc519523027887079a6ec1a267a37b8f23",
    "verification/offline_guard_fault.c": "83c09cfbeca1a247cc8b9a398bf723928fb42d2ac049ef866bdb47bca1c1340e",
    "verification/tla/OfflineCleanup.tla": "602f5b50ecd4e1837ed42e3e11aa447516179836dfb0e31ca924f20541490835",
    "verification/tla/EnvironmentOffline.tla": "dcfbfb561d04eee0f309f352ee4ff926291d26a4f69532d945571df584bcc788"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Fresh-open NotFound must be truthful and shared owners must have persistent layout markers. The environment-only TLA control exposes failure when open falsely reports absence. This is not an unconditional guarantee against arbitrary filesystem misreporting.",
    "The caller must establish actual quiescence and stable namespace bindings through final check/deletion. The Boolean all_participants_stopped is an assertion, not a fencing or process-liveness protocol.",
    "The full historical root closure, Python JSON/traversal, path resolution, report equality and syscall correspondence remain unproved. OfflineCleanup abstracts one physical pack and allows failed deletion with effects; termination includes refusal, not automatic eventual reclamation of all orphans.",
    "Only Python production code changes. The identical native binary and all 21 Verus inputs are checked; 119 positive checks are fresh. The 105 semantic negatives and 40 native tests are reused from exact inputs, not reported as new runs.",
    "Probe phases retain exact Python/native/shim hashes. The baseline intentional private data loss, normal catalog GC and manual legacy fixture teardown are separate evidence categories. The fixed four-host cleanup call uses an unvalidated report; regression tests separately cover a genuinely earlier report followed by marker creation.",
    "Fault injection does not establish a natural stale-stat rate, latency bound or bandwidth guarantee. Full verification and four-host probes overlap; background load/caches are uncontrolled.",
    "No new 100 GB/physical TB workload, complete I/O refinement, repair of historical losses or full-system bug-free claim."
  ],
